    affiliation: "J.D. Candidate, 2027, University of Arizona James E. Rogers College of Law"
type: dataset
date-released: "2026-08-02"
url: "https://github.com/NickGillArizona/Duty-Without-Data"
repository-code: "https://github.com/NickGillArizona/Duty-Without-Data"
abstract: >-
  Replication archive for the law-review Note "Duty Without Data: Disability
  Fair Housing and the Record-Dependent Right." Contains the Note, the FHA
  Unified Database (3,366 federal FHA litigation records; 2,690 screened-in; 1,900
  disability-screened), the multi-model LLM classification pipeline,
  race-by-disability housing cost-burden cross-tabulations from ACS PUMS,
  HUD administrative-system analyses (CDBG, REAC / NSPIRE, POSH), validation
  audits, and the doctrinal-audit methodology and source registers behind the
  Note's footnotes (the underlying working memoranda are retained in the
  project's private research records).
keywords:
  - fair housing act
  - disability
  - AFFH
  - empirical legal studies
  - LLM classification
  - composition effect
  - housing cost burden
  - replication archive
  - census pums
